      "side": 1,
      "message": "No need to list this as it is implied by `m com.androd.art`.\n\nBut this kind of change requires a boot test where you should make sure that the dexpreopt files for apex system server jars are used, and the jars are not dexopted. This can be done e.g. by grepping logcat on first boot making sure that there are no class loader context mismatch errors, something like this:\n\n Test: First boot uses dexpreopt for apex system server jars.\n  In one terminal:\n    $ lunch aosp_cf_x86_64_phone-userdebug \u0026\u0026 m \u0026\u0026 launch_cvd\n  In another terminal:\n    $ adb wait-for-device \u0026\u0026 adb root \u0026\u0026 adb logcat \\\n      | grep -E \u0027ClassLoaderContext [a-z ]+ mismatch\u0027\n      # empty grep output, no errors",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "6a6198d4c5a2d9bbddb9692c199a1071d95dfa9f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
